rget's (ctx, id string), main's rename of getOCIMappings\u2192lib.ConvertCRIToOCIMappings (target still has local getOCIMappings \u2014 keep target's), main's sysfs 'rro' option change and AddNames layer naming (not part of the fix diff \u2014 ignore). (4) runtimehandler-keyed vs sandbox-keyed caches: the fix's caches are keyed by sandbox ID (obtained from SandboxInfo.ID()) and the SandboxInfo interface is exactly satisfied by *sandbox.Sandbox (which has RuntimeHandler() and ID() on target) and by sandboxBuilder once the fix's RuntimeHandler() getter is added \u2014 the Builder interface change is small and portable since target's sandboxRef already stores runtimeHandler. (5) Generated file: test/mocks/ociartifact/datastore/datastore.go is MockGen output whose upstream content reflects main's rewritten datastore interfaces \u2014 regenerating on target produces a different (Impl-only) mock; the new image_vm.go/runtime_vm.go tests do not use datastoremock, so skipping regeneration is safe. (6) The mock-based new tests (image_mgr_test.go, runtime_mgr_test.go) rely only on criostoragemock/containerstoragemock mocks that exist unchanged on target, plus the existing internal/storage/suite_test.go framework variable t \u2014 they should port with minimal edits (the tests call GetImageServiceManager/GetRuntimeServiceManager/HeuristicallyTryResolvingStringAsIDPrefix on the adapted API). (7) The full short unit-test suite currently has exactly ONE failure on the clean target tree: TestAddOCIBindsRROMountsError/should_fail_to_add_an_RRO_mount_without_private_propagation, which is environmental (/ is a private mount, not shared). It is unrelated to the PR (upstream fixed the test guard in commit 94ca4ece6, outside the merge); since the completion bar demands a green suite, port that small test-only guard. (8) The PR also includes a genuinely related test fix (container_events_test.go race via sync.WaitGroup + GinkgoRecover) that should be kept, and unneeded infra (kata ansible