  "reasoning": "This is a large feature merge (24 sub-commits, ~2.6k insertions) that introduces a whole new storage-service abstraction layer: ImageServiceManager/RuntimeServiceManager wrap the existing ImageServer/RuntimeServer and route to per-sandbox runtimePulledImageService/runtimePulledRuntimeService when the runtime handler has runtime_pull_image=true. Key facts verified against the target tree: (1) internal/storage image.go/runtime.go/image_id.go are byte-identical between target and the fix base, so the new image_vm.go/runtime_vm.go implementations of the existing ImageServer/RuntimeServer interfaces will compile nearly as-is; the needed vendor APIs (Store.ContainerRunDirectory, signature.PolicyContext.IsRunningImageAllowed, image.UnparsedInstanceWithReference, oci layout, manifest, cri-api ImageSpec.GetRuntimeHandler) are all present on target. (2) The hard part is internal/ociartifact/datastore: main's fix adds PullManifestOnly/ImageSource/List/Remove/PullConfig + an Artifact wrapper on top of a libartifact-direct datastore (commit 99520fec9) that does NOT exist on release-1.36; these must be re-implemented against target's ociartifact.Store (which already gives List/Remove/Status and an ociartifact.Artifact with Reference/CanonicalName/Digest/RootPath \u2014 the new datastore.Artifact wrapper is redundant on target and should be dropped in favor of returning []*ociartifact.Artifact), and PullManifestOnly/PullConfig/ImageSource written fresh using target's vendored go.podman.io/image/v5 manifest/layout/none-cache APIs, leaving PullData/EnforceConfigMediaType untouched. (3) ~52 call sites of StorageImageServer()/StorageRuntimeServer() across 18 files must change to the new (sb) + error signature; the diff already contains the exact adaptation for each one (mostly mechanical: fetch service once, check err, use local variable), but several target-vs-main drifts must be reconciled by hand: sandbox_run_linux.go setPodSandboxMountLabel(ctx, sbox Builder) vs ta